Back off with jitter when a syncer client reconnects.

A syncer client that loses its connection reconnects after a fixed 2 seconds, with
no backoff or jitter. When many raylets lose the GCS at once they all retry in
lockstep, and every retry makes the GCS send each of them the full cluster view
again, which can keep the connections breaking.

The delay is now exponential backoff with full jitter: uniform between zero and a
ceiling that starts at RAY_ray_syncer_reconnect_base_delay_ms (2000, the previous
fixed delay) and doubles per consecutive failure up to
RAY_ray_syncer_reconnect_max_delay_ms (60000). The count resets once the
connection receives a message.

Upstream status: not yet reported to ray-project/ray.

